# Secrets — never commit. The pipeline reads these from the environment;
# in GitHub Actions they come from repository secrets, not from a file.
.env
.env.*
*.env
.env~
.envrc
!.env*.example

# Credential files that tooling drops into a repo. The Google Cloud console
# downloads client_secret_*.json, and Google's OAuth libraries conventionally
# write token.json / credentials.json. The Gmail OAuth guide that produced
# them is gone, but the rules stay: a key file is cheap to ignore and
# expensive to commit.
# A filename denylist can never be complete. The backstops are the gitleaks
# job in .github/workflows/secret-scan.yml and GitHub push protection.
secrets.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
secrets.toml
/secrets/
credentials*.json
client_secret*.json
token.json
*.pem
*.key

# Logs. A redirected run (`python -m src.pipeline evening > run.log 2>&1`)
# lands here, and `git add .` would commit it.
*.log
/logs/
nohup.out

# Run artifacts. Anchored with a leading slash so a tests/fixtures/results/
# directory elsewhere in the tree is not swallowed too. archive() writes
# results/ on every run; render_chart() writes charts/ whenever a candidate
# clears the 2LYNCH gate.
/results/
/charts/

# The charts the pipeline really writes today (src/pipeline.py's CHARTS_DIR).
# NOT covered by /charts/ above — that rule is anchored to the repo root, and
# `git check-ignore -v docs/charts/AAPL.png` said so — and nothing was ever
# committed there only because evening.yml's persist step was aborting before
# its commit on every run. Once that was fixed this became ~57 KB a chart, up
# to 25 a night: about 360 MB a year of history that does not delta-compress
# and cannot be taken back out afterwards. The page says where the image went
# (docs/index.html's chartSlot) and the evening email still carries the PNGs
# it just rendered, from the local filesystem.
#
# Anchored and directory-only on purpose. This project has twice shipped a
# .gitignore round that swallowed source — src/env/loader.py and
# tests/fixtures/results/ — so the rule names one directory under the repo
# root and nothing else.
/docs/charts/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Virtualenvs. Anchored: an `env/` package elsewhere in the tree is source.
/.venv/
/venv/
/env/

# Agent tooling scratch space (git worktrees created for parallel work).
.claude/worktrees/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
